================================================================================
  Lead game server installed under /usr/local/lead

  The post-install step has already (best effort):
    * created the dedicated 'lead' user/group (home = /usr/local/lead)
    * built the in-tree symlinks + runtime dirs
    * autodiscovered this host's IP and wrote it as bind_ip in the core configs
    * enabled & started MariaDB and created the databases + migrations
    * enabled the service (lead_enable=YES)

  Everything is driven by ONE command: lead-ctl (in /usr/local/sbin, on PATH).

      lead-ctl start            # start everything (db, auth, mark, ch1-4, ch99)
      lead-ctl start ch2        # start ONLY channel 2
      lead-ctl stop ch4         # stop ONLY channel 4
      lead-ctl restart ch1
      lead-ctl status
      lead-ctl backup [dir]     # full backup: all DBs + serverfiles (-> /var/backups/lead)
      lead-ctl migrate          # create DBs + apply new migrations (idempotent)
      lead-ctl configure        # re-autodiscover the host IP into the configs
      lead-ctl update           # update to a newer GitHub release if available

  Core configs are @config files (preserved across upgrades); review the
  autodetected address / DB credentials if needed:

      /usr/local/lead/auth/CONFIG
      /usr/local/lead/channel1/game1/CONFIG   (and game2, channel2-4, channel99)
      /usr/local/lead/db/conf.txt

  At boot, the rc service uses lead_channels from rc.conf (default "1 2 3 4"):

      sysrc lead_enable=YES ; service lead start

  Logs live under /usr/local/lead/<core>/{syserr.txt,log/}.
================================================================================
